<title>POLAND: POLISH NBP REJECTS ALL BIDS AT ITS 3-DAY REVREPO.</title>
<headline>POLISH NBP REJECTS ALL BIDS AT ITS 3-DAY REVREPO.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland rejected all bids at its three-day reverse repo after banks bid to place 70 million with the bank against a 300 million zloty offer, the NBP said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday the bank drained the market for one day at 21.30 percent and a Reuter poll on Thursday showed dealers expected the NBP to raise the maximum accepted rate to about 23 percent at today's operation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
